From 0f8b8e0a608affe5bcfb665e73ea55b0f2821be5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 02:06:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): host sync belongs to the root profile gateway;
 heal released inherited creator links [daveey]

Hub chats 20261016_123957_6212f7 and 20261017_114040_587d59 read unresolved/no_summary though they handed work to
open cards (t_01a19084a3b36956 todo; decision card t_c21c170e). Their chat links were released=1, so session_tasks
returned nothing. Five whys:
- hermes-gateway-askeve-reviewer (named profile, pinned older core, no origin ledger in its HERMES_HOME) won the
  first-come host .sync.lock and its links reconcile released inherited created links and every root-profile
  ledger link each pass;
- the root gateway logged 'another gateway already syncs; not starting' and never retried;
- reconcile kept an inherited created link's stored released flag, so the root's own reconcile could not heal it.

Fix: a named-profile gateway leaves host sync to a live root-profile gateway (and hands the loop back when one
starts); a contended lock is retried instead of abandoned; reconcile wants an owned card's inherited created link
unreleased (a picked-up foreign copy keeps the owner's answer). Tests per path.
